# Binaries
bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
Dockerfile.cross

# Test artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
coverage
cover*.out
*.coverprofile

# Go workspace
go.work
go.work.sum

# Build artifacts
dist/

# Generated Kubernetes files (keep vendored)
!vendor/**/zz_generated.*

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.codex
# Claude commands and skills are shared project tooling and are checked in;
# only genuinely per-developer state (settings.local.json) and scratch
# (worktrees/) stays local. .specify/ already tracks the spec-kit engine —
# templates, scripts, constitution — so leaving the commands that drive it
# agent-local meant a fresh clone got the engine with no way to run it. That
# is exactly how the spec-kit skills went missing once already.
#
# Anything added under .claude/commands/ or .claude/skills/ is committed by
# default. Keep personal experiments outside those directories, or in your
# user-level ~/.claude.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/skills/
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.continue/
.aider*
# Codex integration skills are shared project tooling. Keep other agent state
# local, matching the tracked-skill policy above for Claude.
.agents/*
!.agents/skills/
!.agents/skills/**

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local junk
.cache/
.gocache

# Design docs (local-only)
DESIGN.md

# Graphify
# Commit the rendered graph (graph.json, graph.html, GRAPH_REPORT.md,
# manifest.json) so any agent or contributor has the same map without
# re-running extraction. Keep transient work files, the per-developer cache,
# and cost telemetry out.
/.graphify_*
graphify-out/.*
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/cost.json
